 "sq": [
  {
   "_id": 18785,
   "ANSWER": "<p><br data-end=\"1664\" data-start=\"1661\" />\nImplicit threading refers to <strong data-end=\"1717\" data-start=\"1693\">automatic management</strong> of threads by <strong data-end=\"1758\" data-start=\"1732\">compilers or libraries</strong> instead of programmers. It simplifies development by hiding thread creation, synchronization, and management, and improves scalability in parallel applications.</p>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSC202J",
   "LEVEL": 1,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO1",
    "PLO2"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<h3 data-end=\"1649\" data-start=\"1589\"><strong data-end=\"1647\" data-start=\"1593\">What is implicit threading, and why is it used?</strong></h3>\n\n<p data-end=\"1919\" data-start=\"1650\">&nbsp;</p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 208,
   "TYPE": "sq",
   "key": 18785
  },
  {
   "_id": 18786,
   "ANSWER": "<p data-end=\"2012\" data-start=\"1999\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<ol data-end=\"2301\" data-start=\"2013\">\n\t<li data-end=\"2155\" data-start=\"2013\">\n\t<p data-end=\"2155\" data-start=\"2016\"><strong data-end=\"2034\" data-start=\"2016\">Race Condition</strong> &ndash; Occurs when two or more threads access shared data simultaneously, and the output depends on the sequence of access.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"2301\" data-start=\"2156\">\n\t<p data-end=\"2301\" data-start=\"2159\"><strong data-end=\"2171\" data-start=\"2159\">Deadlock</strong> &ndash; Happens when two or more threads are waiting indefinitely for resources held by each other, resulting in a complete standstill.</p>\n\t</li>\n</ol>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSC202J",
   "LEVEL": 2,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO2",
    "PLO3"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<h3 data-end=\"1998\" data-start=\"1926\"><strong data-end=\"1996\" data-start=\"1930\">List two common threading issues and briefly describe them.</strong></h3>\n\n<p data-end=\"2012\" data-start=\"1999\">\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 208,
   "TYPE": "sq",
   "key": 18786
  }
 ],
 "lq": [
  {
   "_id": 18787,
   "ANSWER": "<p data-end=\"2830\" data-start=\"2607\"><strong data-end=\"2629\" data-start=\"2607\">Implicit threading</strong> is a programming approach where the <strong data-end=\"2722\" data-start=\"2666\">creation, scheduling, and synchronization of threads</strong> are handled by the <strong data-end=\"2789\" data-start=\"2742\">compiler, runtime environment, or libraries</strong>, rather than manually by the programmer.</p>\n\n<h3 data-end=\"2879\" data-start=\"2837\"><strong data-end=\"2879\" data-start=\"2841\">Techniques for Implicit Threading:</strong></h3>\n\n<ol data-end=\"3471\" data-start=\"2881\">\n\t<li data-end=\"2993\" data-start=\"2881\">\n\t<p data-end=\"2903\" data-start=\"2884\"><strong data-end=\"2901\" data-start=\"2884\">Thread Pools:</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"2993\" data-start=\"2907\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"2954\" data-start=\"2907\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"2954\" data-start=\"2909\">Pre-created threads ready to execute tasks.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"2993\" data-start=\"2958\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"2993\" data-start=\"2960\">Reduces thread creation overhead.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"3156\" data-start=\"2995\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3035\" data-start=\"2998\"><strong data-end=\"3033\" data-start=\"2998\">OpenMP (Open Multi-Processing):</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"3156\" data-start=\"3039\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"3076\" data-start=\"3039\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"3076\" data-start=\"3041\">A compiler directive-based model.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"3156\" data-start=\"3080\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"3156\" data-start=\"3082\">Example: <code data-end=\"3117\" data-start=\"3091\">#pragma omp parallel for</code> for automatic parallel loops in C/C++.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"3310\" data-start=\"3158\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3196\" data-start=\"3161\"><strong data-end=\"3194\" data-start=\"3161\">Grand Central Dispatch (GCD):</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"3310\" data-start=\"3200\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"3265\" data-start=\"3200\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"3265\" data-start=\"3202\">Used in macOS/iOS for managing tasks on multicore processors.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"3310\" data-start=\"3269\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"3310\" data-start=\"3271\">Uses queues and system-managed threads.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"3471\" data-start=\"3312\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3353\" data-start=\"3315\"><strong data-end=\"3351\" data-start=\"3315\">TBB (Threading Building Blocks):</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"3471\" data-start=\"3357\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"3409\" data-start=\"3357\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"3409\" data-start=\"3359\">Intel library for task-based parallelism in C++.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"3471\" data-start=\"3413\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"3471\" data-start=\"3415\">Automatically distributes tasks among available threads.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3 data-end=\"3519\" data-start=\"3478\"><strong data-end=\"3519\" data-start=\"3482\">Advantages of Implicit Threading:</strong></h3>\n\n<ul data-end=\"3755\" data-start=\"3521\">\n\t<li data-end=\"3589\" data-start=\"3521\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3589\" data-start=\"3523\"><strong data-end=\"3549\" data-start=\"3523\">Simplifies development</strong> by hiding low-level thread operations</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"3636\" data-start=\"3590\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3636\" data-start=\"3592\"><strong data-end=\"3617\" data-start=\"3592\">Increases portability</strong> across platforms</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"3686\" data-start=\"3637\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3686\" data-start=\"3639\"><strong data-end=\"3663\" data-start=\"3639\">Improves scalability</strong> on multicore systems</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"3755\" data-start=\"3687\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3755\" data-start=\"3689\"><strong data-end=\"3714\" data-start=\"3689\">Optimizes performance</strong> using runtime systems and load balancing</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 data-end=\"3794\" data-start=\"3762\"><strong data-end=\"3794\" data-start=\"3766\">Common Threading Issues:</strong></h3>\n\n<h4 data-end=\"3826\" data-start=\"3796\">1. <strong data-end=\"3824\" data-start=\"3804\">Race Conditions:</strong></h4>\n\n<ul data-end=\"4034\" data-start=\"3827\">\n\t<li data-end=\"3892\" data-start=\"3827\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3892\" data-start=\"3829\">Occurs when multiple threads access shared data concurrently.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"3964\" data-start=\"3893\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3964\" data-start=\"3895\">Results in <strong data-end=\"3932\" data-start=\"3906\">unpredictable behavior</strong> depending on execution order.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"4034\" data-start=\"3965\">\n\t<p data-end=\"4034\" data-start=\"3967\">Requires <strong data-end=\"4006\" data-start=\"3976\">synchronization mechanisms</strong> like mutexes or semaphores.</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h4 data-end=\"4060\" data-start=\"4036\">2. <strong data-end=\"4058\" data-start=\"4044\">Deadlocks:</strong></h4>\n\n<ul data-end=\"4214\" data-start=\"4061\">\n\t<li data-end=\"4123\" data-start=\"4061\">\n\t<p data-end=\"4123\" data-start=\"4063\">When threads wait indefinitely for each other&rsquo;s resources.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"4214\" data-start=\"4124\">\n\t<p data-end=\"4214\" data-start=\"4126\">Prevented using resource ordering, timeout mechanisms, or deadlock detection algorithms.</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h4 data-end=\"4241\" data-start=\"4216\">3. <strong data-end=\"4239\" data-start=\"4224\">Starvation:</strong></h4>\n\n<ul data-end=\"4426\" data-start=\"4242\">\n\t<li data-end=\"4347\" data-start=\"4242\">\n\t<p data-end=\"4347\" data-start=\"4244\">A thread waits indefinitely due to <strong data-end=\"4306\" data-start=\"4279\">lack of resource access</strong> or being <strong data-end=\"4344\" data-start=\"4316\">ignored by the scheduler</strong>.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"4426\" data-start=\"4348\">\n\t<p data-end=\"4426\" data-start=\"4350\">Occurs when resources are consistently allocated to higher-priority threads.</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h4 data-end=\"4461\" data-start=\"4428\">4. <strong data-end=\"4459\" data-start=\"4436\">Priority Inversion:</strong></h4>\n\n<ul data-end=\"4581\" data-start=\"4462\">\n\t<li data-end=\"4581\" data-start=\"4462\">\n\t<p data-end=\"4581\" data-start=\"4464\">A lower-priority thread holds a resource needed by a higher-priority thread, but cannot release it due to scheduling.</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n",
